Sort by start, then sweep merging overlaps. O(n log n).

For merge intervals basic I will sort intervals and merge overlapping consecutive pairs.

```python
def merge(intervals):
    intervals.sort()
    out = []
    for s, e in intervals:
        if out and s <= out[-1][1]:
            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)
        else:
            out.append([s, e])
    return out
```

